{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000061-playing-aliens-in-cwod","id":1000061,"title":"Playing Aliens in cWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T18:06:03-08:00","id":1000061,"title":"Playing Aliens in cWoD","content":"I was wondering if anyone had designed rules for playing hidden extraterrestrials in cWoD. I imagine that they would have to be able to hide their nature effectively and would have access to advanced technology, but I think that most of the UFO stuff would be too obvious and too stupid to reflect 'real' Aliens. What would you suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:20:29-08:00","id":1000431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000061-playing-aliens-in-cwod#post1000061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if anyone had designed rules for playing hidden extraterrestrials in cWoD. I imagine that they would have to be able to hide their nature effectively and would have access to advanced technology, but I think that most of the UFO stuff would be too obvious and too stupid to reflect 'real' Aliens. What would you suggest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds cool. You could replicate them with Bygone Bestiary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:31:38-08:00","id":1000465,"title":"","content":"im very into the UFO mythos and conspiracies, so if ya need help with &quot;Races.&quot; and such, let me know","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:58:30-08:00","id":1000487,"title":"","content":"Cool, I appreciate the support. I was thinking of dividing them by heritage (alien, hybrid, or minion), policy (colonization, experimentation, or observation), race (mammalian, avian, reptilian, amphibian, or piscine), and technology (magical technology, psychic technology, or scientific technology).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T04:37:37-08:00","id":1001712,"title":"","content":"Well the first thing we need to address is that, whether the UFO stuff with the grays is silly or not, they are canon in the cWoD. They're called the Ka Luon. The Void Engineers have dealings with them frequently, and it's more or less implied that their LERMUS were fashioned from Ka Luon genetic material. Combine that with how the grays are well supported by human Mythic Threads, and it's not something that can just be written off.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the idea of having a bunch of different aliens, and a bunch of different policies, technologies, etc.<br /> <br /> But the very same thing that helps the Ka Luon exist - Mythic Threads and belief - also make it difficult for aliens to run around Earth. Disbelief taxes their bodies just like any Bygone. The only ways around this would either be 1) the aliens have a consistent source of Quintessence to draw from, or 2) the alien beings play close to the idea of &quot;hidden extraterrestrials&quot; and make themselves look human enough that the Consensus doesn't reject them. So kind of like what the Changelings do, except less chimerical.<br /> <br /> They could wear complex human suits, like in V or Men In Black. Or they could make like Loma Shade from Shade The Changing Girl or the Great Race of Yith from Lovecraft, and be aliens who abandoned their original bodies in order to astral project and possess human ones. Or they could use some kind of sophisticated cloaking technology, so their bodies look human. Or they genetically modify themselves (if they aren't hybrids already) to look human, enough that most people see their more inhuman features and dismiss them as makeup or birth defects (Star Trek has gone a long way towards &quot;normalizing&quot; the idea of rubber forehead aliens).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:52:53-08:00","id":1001727,"title":"","content":"I would think that they would have to disquiet their appearance. Given the appearance of Greys, I would imagine that they were actually human-amphibian alien hybrids, but the Greys could be something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:35:30-08:00","id":1002579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000061-playing-aliens-in-cwod?p=1001712#post1001712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they could make like Loma Shade from Shade The Changing Girl or the Great Race of Yith from Lovecraft, and be aliens who abandoned their original bodies in order to astral project and possess human ones. Or they could use some kind of sophisticated cloaking technology, so their bodies look human. Or they genetically modify themselves (if they aren't hybrids already) to look human, enough that most people see their more inhuman features and dismiss them as makeup or birth defects (Star Trek has gone a long way towards &quot;normalizing&quot; the idea of rubber forehead aliens).</div> </div> </div> </div>It occurs to me that the Werewolf supplement <b>Freak Legion</b> could go a long way toward generating characters that fit these descriptions without requiring much homebrew. Hell, what if werewolves have it completely wrong about what fomori <i>are</i>?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}